<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.pragmatica-lite</groupId>
        <artifactId>pragmatica</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0-rc4</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>test-plan-witness</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>Test Plan Witness</name>
    <description>
        A JUnit Platform listener that leaves a marker file in the reports directory for as long as a
        test plan is executing. A marker that outlives the fork is proof the plan never finished.
    </description>

    <!--
        WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS (#1344).

        A surefire fork can end a test plan early and still exit 0 with a clean goodbye. Observed on
        2026-09-19: a StackOverflowError bottomed out inside java.lang.StringBuffer's static
        initialiser, poisoning the class for the JVM's lifetime; when the failing test was later
        reported, surefire's own listener threw NoClassDefFoundError while writing the failure, JUnit's
        attempt to log THAT threw the same error, the Throwable escaped the launcher, and
        ForkedBooter.execute() caught it, failed to report it (the report path needs the same class)
        and then said goodbye from its finally block: BYE, System.exit(0), BUILD SUCCESS. Five classes
        never ran. Neither surefire 3.5.1 nor 3.5.4 has a setting for "the fork said goodbye before
        the plan finished".

        The witness turns that silence into evidence that is present BEFORE anything can go wrong:
        the marker is written when the plan starts and removed only when
        TestExecutionListener.testPlanExecutionFinished is reached, which JUnit does not call from a
        finally block. Whatever kills the plan, the marker stays. The root pom's test-plan-gate
        profile fails the module when a marker or a fork dump survives the test phase.

        This module must depend on NOTHING in this repository: every module with src/test pulls it
        in at test scope through that profile, so a dependency on core would be a reactor cycle. For
        the same reason it has no src/test of its own (the profile would make it depend on itself);
        its pins live in script-gate.
    -->

    <properties>
        <!-- Build-instrument module: never published. -->
        <maven.deploy.skip>true</maven.deploy.skip>
        <gpg.skip>true</gpg.skip>
        <jbct.skip>false</jbct.skip>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- Surefire and failsafe put the launcher on the fork's classpath themselves. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.platform</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-platform-launcher</artifactId>
            <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</project>
